course: dictionary
lesson: 5507
title: Words for doing nothing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To laze means to relax and do nothing much, in a lazy but pleasant way. You might laze on the sofa on a Sunday, or laze in the sun on holiday. Lazing is resting and enjoying yourself.
explain: Be careful: laze and lazy are not the same. Lazy means you do not want to work when you should. Laze can be a happy, sensible choice. Common phrases are «laze about», «laze around» and «laze in the sun».
explain: The poem says, «Or frowst with a book by the fire». Frowst means to laze in a stuffy, warm room, so the poem warns us that sitting still is not the cure for the hump. The next line, «But to take a large hoe and a shovel also», shows we should work outside instead.
explain: Use the context check. Put laze in place of frowst: «Or laze with a book by the fire» still makes sense, so your meaning fits the poem.
fact: To laze means to relax and do nothing much, in a lazy, pleasant way.
fact: Laze is a verb: laze, lazes, lazed, lazing.
fact: Phrases with laze include «laze about», «laze around» and «laze in the sun».
fact: Lazing is resting; «lazy» means not wanting to work when you should.
fact: «Frowst» means to laze in a stuffy, warm room, as in «Or frowst with a book by the fire».
exercise: The poem says «Or frowst with a book by the fire». What does frowst mean here? | *To laze in a stuffy, warm room | To run fast around the garden | To sing loudly | To dig a hole with a shovel
exercise: Which phrase uses laze to mean relax with nothing much to do? | *Laze around | Take a large hoe | Dig till you gently perspire | Shovel the soil
exercise: What is the past tense of laze? | Lazing | Lazes | *Lazed
test: Is it always bad to laze? | Only on school days | Only when you are ill | *No, lazing can be a pleasant rest | Yes, lazing is always wrong
test: Which word means not wanting to work when you should? | Pleasant | Relaxed | *Lazy | Warm
exam: What is the difference between laze and lazy? | Laze and lazy mean exactly the same thing | Laze means to work hard, while lazy means to rest | Lazy is a colour and laze is a place | *Laze is pleasant resting, while lazy means not wanting to work when you should
